00:47:44.200 --> 00:47:45.240
We were crossboarding?
我们当时是在交叉拍摄吗？

1102
00:47:45.240 --> 00:47:46.840
Yes, at the same time.
是的，同时进行。

1103
00:47:46.960 --> 00:47:48.800
This was because of Amy Ryan's schedule.
这是因为艾米·瑞恩的档期问题。

1104
00:47:49.060 --> 00:47:51.480
So, we had to group all of her work together.
所以我们必须把她的戏份集中在一起拍。

1105
00:47:51.760 --> 00:47:58.640
In one day, we would go from traditional Christmas to classy Christmas to regular bullpen with
在一天之内，我们要从传统圣诞场景切换到高级圣诞场景，再到没有圣诞装饰的常规办公区，

1106
00:47:58.640 --> 00:48:01.600
no Christmas and then back to a Christmas again.
然后再切回圣诞场景。

1107
00:48:01.860 --> 00:48:02.220
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1108
00:48:02.220 --> 00:48:04.900
And there would be little lines that would say, change over.
而且会有小字条写着，换场。

1109
00:48:05.080 --> 00:48:06.640
Change over to classy Christmas.
换成高级圣诞场景。

1110
00:48:06.740 --> 00:48:09.240
And we'd go off to the parking lot or something.
然后我们就得去停车场之类的地方待着。

1111
00:48:09.240 --> 00:48:11.560
And they would have to redecorate all of that.
他们得把所有场景重新布置一遍。

1112
00:48:11.560 --> 00:48:13.920
Like, four times in one day.
一天之内要换四次。

1113
00:48:14.060 --> 00:48:14.160
Wow.
哇。

1114
00:48:14.160 --> 00:48:15.400
It was bonkers.
真是疯了。

1115
00:48:15.820 --> 00:48:16.140
Wow.
哇。

1116
00:48:16.720 --> 00:48:16.900
Geez.
天呐。

1117
00:48:17.140 --> 00:48:19.680
See, those are those things we talk about that goes on behind the scenes.
你看，这就是我们常说的幕后工作。

1118
00:48:19.680 --> 00:48:21.860
That's just like, it just happens.
事情就是这样发生的。

1119
00:48:22.040 --> 00:48:22.660
It just happens.
就是这样。

1120
00:48:23.440 --> 00:48:26.680
I do have a question for you all, Jenna, Sam, and Cassie.
我有个问题想问你们大家，珍娜、萨姆和卡西。

1121
00:48:26.960 --> 00:48:31.780
Are you traditional Christmas or are you classy Christmas in your decorating?
你们在装饰圣诞节时，是走传统风格还是高级风格？

1122
00:48:32.300 --> 00:48:33.960
I am traditional Christmas.
我是传统圣诞风格。

1123
00:48:34.420 --> 00:48:36.940
Sorry, Cassie said traditional and I had the mic on.
抱歉，卡西说了传统风格，而我正好开着麦。

1124
00:48:37.600 --> 00:48:39.360
I need a ruling from you guys.
我需要你们帮我评判一下。

1125
00:48:39.520 --> 00:48:43.700
The past decade, every year, I do a big pink Dolly Parton tree.
过去十年，我每年都会装饰一棵巨大的粉色桃莉·巴顿风格圣诞树。

1126
00:48:43.700 --> 00:48:44.600
You're retro Christmas.
你是复古圣诞风格。

1127
00:48:44.800 --> 00:48:45.100
Is that what it is?
是这样吗？

1128
00:48:45.100 --> 00:48:46.400
You're retro Christmas, yeah.
你是复古圣诞风格，没错。

1129
00:48:46.500 --> 00:48:46.620
Yeah.
是的。

1130
00:48:46.960 --> 00:48:47.200
100%.
百分之百。

1131
00:48:47.200 --> 00:48:48.460
I love your pink tree.
我喜欢你的粉色圣诞树。

1132
00:48:48.580 --> 00:48:48.880
Thank you.
谢谢。

1133
00:48:49.240 --> 00:48:49.800
Yes.
没错。

1134
00:48:49.960 --> 00:48:52.880
I am traditional Christmas as well.
我也是传统圣诞风格。

1135
00:48:53.240 --> 00:48:56.120
But I love a bonus tree.
但我喜欢额外再多摆一棵树。

1136
00:48:56.480 --> 00:48:58.060
Like, a little extra little tree.
比如，一棵小巧的圣诞树。

1137
00:48:58.260 --> 00:49:00.400
Like, I have a miniature hot pink tree.
就像我有一棵迷你的亮粉色圣诞树。

1138
00:49:00.660 --> 00:49:01.420
You know?
你知道吗？

1139
00:49:01.600 --> 00:49:02.600
Maybe I'm a combo.
也许我是混合风格。

1140
00:49:02.880 --> 00:49:04.420
But I'm not classy Christmas.
但我不是那种高级圣诞风格。

1141
00:49:04.420 --> 00:49:08.140
I'm not like white feathers and silver balls and things.
我不是那种用白色羽毛、银色球装饰之类的风格。

1142
00:49:09.580 --> 00:49:10.060
What?
什么？

1143
00:49:11.300 --> 00:49:12.760
You know what I'm talking about?
你知道我在说什么吗？

1144
00:49:13.860 --> 00:49:14.680
Come on.
得了吧。

1145
00:49:15.460 --> 00:49:16.540
You know, stop it.
你知道的，别闹了。

1146
00:49:17.560 --> 00:49:19.200
I do know what you're talking about.
我确实知道你在说什么。

1147
00:49:19.340 --> 00:49:19.680
I don't know.
我不知道。

1148
00:49:19.900 --> 00:49:20.760
I don't know.
我不知道。

1149
00:49:20.980 --> 00:49:23.040
It's just fluff or nutter all over again.
这简直又是重演了一次“棉花糖还是花生酱”的争论。

1150
00:49:24.320 --> 00:49:29.640
Well, anyway, I guess we have three traditional Christmas here and one retro Christmas.
好吧，总之，我想我们这里有三位是传统圣诞风格，一位是复古圣诞风格。

1151
00:49:30.580 --> 00:49:36.300
Next, we have a scene that I have as a question mark for several reasons.
接下来这个场景，我因为几个原因给它打了个问号。

1152
00:49:36.600 --> 00:49:36.800
Okay.
好的。

1153
00:49:36.800 --> 00:49:39.320
It's a big, long talking head from Michael.
这是迈克尔一段很长、很啰嗦的访谈。

1154
00:49:40.120 --> 00:49:45.080
He's in his new, snazzy Santa outfit.
他穿着那套时髦的新圣诞老人装。

1155
00:49:45.400 --> 00:49:46.780
I'm calling it sassy Santa.
我管它叫俏皮圣诞老人。

1156
00:49:46.780 --> 00:49:47.300
Okay.
好的。

1157
00:49:47.880 --> 00:49:53.340
And while he's delivering this talking head, it is slowly revealed that Angela is hemming his pants.
在他进行这段访谈时，镜头慢慢揭示出安吉拉正在给他缝裤脚。

1158
00:49:53.900 --> 00:49:56.340
It was not in our original shooting draft.
这在最初的拍摄剧本里是没有的。

1159
00:49:56.640 --> 00:49:57.220
I know.
我知道。

1160
00:49:57.320 --> 00:50:01.240
I think it was added because I found it in later pages in a blue revised.
我想这是后来加进去的，因为我在蓝色修订版的后续页面里看到了。

1161
00:50:01.500 --> 00:50:01.740
Okay.
好的。

1162
00:50:01.880 --> 00:50:02.960
I think they added this scene.
我觉得是他们加了这场戏。

1163
00:50:03.500 --> 00:50:05.480
This scene was so much fun.
这场戏拍得太开心了。

1164
00:50:05.640 --> 00:50:10.400
First of all, I love it whenever Michael's in his office and then we reveal someone else has been there all along.
首先，我特别喜欢这种迈克尔在办公室里说话，然后镜头一转揭示出其实一直有人在旁边的桥段。

1165
00:50:10.840 --> 00:50:15.300
And I thought Steve did such a great job of selling the ouch and then it panning down to me.
我觉得史蒂夫演得太棒了，他那种“哎哟”的反应，然后镜头摇到我这里，效果特别好。

1166
00:50:15.820 --> 00:50:23.860
Well, Angela, we have a fan question from Kara P in New Zealand who would like to know if you improvised your last line where you say, yes, he is.
安吉拉，我们收到一个来自新西兰Kara P的粉丝提问，她想知道你最后那句“是的，他是”是不是即兴发挥的。

1167
00:50:24.840 --> 00:50:32.500
Because Kara says, on my millionth rewatch, it stood out to me as sounding like an Angela Kinsey improv, which always make me laugh.
因为Kara说，在她看了无数遍之后，那句台词听起来特别像安吉拉·金赛的即兴创作，每次都能把她逗笑。

1168
00:50:33.480 --> 00:50:34.240
Thanks, Kara.
谢谢你，Kara。

1169
00:50:34.520 --> 00:50:37.380
Well, actually, Steve and I improvised quite a bit in this scene.
其实，史蒂夫和我在这一场戏里即兴发挥了不少。

1170
00:50:37.720 --> 00:50:40.200
So we did the scene as scripted, but kind of loosely.
我们按剧本演了，但演得比较随意。

1171
00:50:40.740 --> 00:50:42.660
But the whole end of it was improv.
结尾整段都是即兴的。

1172
00:50:42.660 --> 00:50:46.840
So as scripted, Michael said, could he help us with some parking tickets?
剧本里，迈克尔问他能不能帮我们处理一些停车罚单？

1173
00:50:47.660 --> 00:50:49.480
And then we improvised the following.
然后我们即兴发挥了接下来的内容。

1174
00:50:49.880 --> 00:50:51.920
Angela says, I don't think that's appropriate.
安吉拉说，我觉得那样不合适。

1175
00:50:52.120 --> 00:50:54.000
And Michael says, well, then he's not a senator.
迈克尔说，那他就不是参议员了。

1176
00:50:54.200 --> 00:50:55.880
And then I said, yes, he is.
然后我说，是的，他是。

1177
00:50:55.960 --> 00:50:57.020
And Michael said, okay.
迈克尔说，好吧。

1178
00:50:58.200 --> 00:51:00.240
So we improvised the whole end of the scene.
所以我们把整场戏的结尾都即兴发挥了。

1179
00:51:00.640 --> 00:51:01.000
Nice.
不错。

1180
00:51:01.300 --> 00:51:02.680
But it was really fun.
但真的很有趣。

1181
00:51:02.860 --> 00:51:08.100
Well, I feel like this is a big character reveal moment as well, which is that you're apparently a good seamstress.
我觉得这也是一个重要的角色揭秘时刻，原来你是个裁缝高手。

1182
00:51:08.300 --> 00:51:09.060
Yes, I so.
是的，我是。

1183
00:51:09.240 --> 00:51:10.200
I believe that, though.
我倒挺相信的。

1184
00:51:10.320 --> 00:51:13.180
I feel like Angela made all of her cat Halloween costumes.
我觉得安吉拉肯定亲手做过她所有猫咪的万圣节服装。

1185
00:51:13.500 --> 00:51:13.760
Yes.
是的。

1186
00:51:13.940 --> 00:51:14.100
Yeah.
没错。

1187
00:51:14.660 --> 00:51:16.020
Well, now we're going to move to the kitchen.
好了，现在我们要转到厨房场景了。

1188
00:51:16.020 --> 00:51:22.060
And we're going to find out that Jim and Pam are going to exchange some presents today at the party.
我们会发现吉姆和帕姆打算在今天的派对上交换礼物。

1189
00:51:22.900 --> 00:51:28.320
Now, I don't know if you noticed, but Jim is wearing an almost identical tie.
不知道你有没有注意到，吉姆戴的领带几乎一模一样。

1190
00:51:28.760 --> 00:51:29.520
I did.
我注意到了。

1191
00:51:29.520 --> 00:51:36.700
It is that same blue on top with the white snow falling, but at the bottom, you see a Santa going into a chimney.
上面还是同样的蓝色配白色雪花，但底部能看到一个圣诞老人正钻进烟囱。

1192
00:51:37.340 --> 00:51:37.780
Yes.
是的。

1193
00:51:38.240 --> 00:51:38.540
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1194
00:51:38.700 --> 00:51:39.000
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1195
00:51:39.160 --> 00:51:46.180
Is this a very popular Christmas tie motif, the blue with snow on top leading to something?
这种蓝色底配顶部雪花、底部有图案的圣诞领带图案很流行吗？

1196
00:51:46.480 --> 00:51:47.420
I feel like it is.
我觉得是的。

1197
00:51:47.500 --> 00:51:51.140
I feel like I've seen this tie with a penguin, like, sliding in some snow at the bottom.
我好像见过这种领带，底部是一只企鹅在雪地里滑行。

1198
00:51:51.140 --> 00:51:51.960
Yes, exactly.
没错，就是那种。

1199
00:51:52.800 --> 00:51:53.240
Hmm.
嗯。

1200
00:51:53.240 --> 00:52:02.240
Well, in the scene with Jim and Pam, Pam kind of plays off like, okay, I didn't have time to really do anything for your present, which clearly means she did something big.
在吉姆和帕姆的这场戏里，帕姆表现得好像是，好吧，我没时间给你准备什么礼物，但这显然意味着她准备了份大礼。

1201
00:52:02.820 --> 00:52:10.220
We find out in her talking head she's been working on this for a really long time, and she has made a comic book starring Jim.
她在访谈中透露，她为此准备了很长时间，还创作了一本以吉姆为主角的漫画书。

1202
00:52:10.520 --> 00:52:15.180
He's a mild-mannered paper salesman who gets bit by a radioactive bear and becomes bear man.
他是一个温文尔雅的纸张推销员，被一只放射性熊咬伤后变成了熊人。

1203
00:52:15.560 --> 00:52:20.680
And, Angela, I have all the details about the making of that comic book, but I'm going to wait.
安吉拉，关于那本漫画书的制作细节我全都知道，但我打算先卖个关子。

1204
00:52:20.840 --> 00:52:22.520
I'm going to share about it next week.
下周再和大家分享。

1205
00:52:22.640 --> 00:52:23.020
Okay.
好的。

1206
00:52:23.240 --> 00:52:26.660
Well, Jim has returned to his desk, and there's a little sticky note.
吉姆回到了办公桌前，上面有一张小便利贴。

1207
00:52:27.880 --> 00:52:28.920
Safety meeting.
安全会议。

1208
00:52:29.280 --> 00:52:32.980
We will be burning a sticky note.
我们要烧掉一张便利贴。

1209
00:52:33.400 --> 00:52:37.400
There is a bucket under the desk with water.
桌子下面放着一桶水。

1210
00:52:37.680 --> 00:52:39.560
This is what our safety meetings were like.
我们的安全会议以前就是这样。

1211
00:52:39.840 --> 00:52:41.540
Also, there would be a whole speech.
而且还会有一大段演讲。

1212
00:52:41.680 --> 00:52:43.720
There will be an open flame.
会有明火。

1213
00:52:44.180 --> 00:52:44.600
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1214
00:52:44.740 --> 00:52:45.120
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1215
00:52:45.480 --> 00:52:48.780
I always wondered what safety meetings are like when there's real stuff.
我一直很好奇，当真的有危险情况时，安全会议会是什么样。

1216
00:52:48.960 --> 00:52:50.780
Like, there's going to be a car crash.
比如，如果真的要发生车祸。

1217
00:52:51.140 --> 00:52:51.540
Yes.
没错。

1218
00:52:51.740 --> 00:52:52.700
Like, what?
比如什么？

1219
00:52:53.260 --> 00:52:54.040
It's true.
这是真的。

1220
00:52:54.460 --> 00:53:00.920
I don't know if you noticed, as Jim is walking to his desk to find the sticky note, it's at 12 minutes and 17 seconds.
不知道你有没有注意到，吉姆走回座位发现便利贴时，时间是12分17秒。

1221
00:53:00.920 --> 00:53:06.960
He walks past the conference room window, and the background scrim out the window.
他走过会议室窗户，背景是窗外的布景。

1222
00:53:06.960 --> 00:53:13.420
First of all, it's not snowing, and the scrim did not represent a snowy day.
首先，当时并没有下雪，那个布景也不是为了表现下雪天。

1223
00:53:13.800 --> 00:53:15.400
It was a little catch.
那是个小穿帮。

1224
00:53:15.400 --> 00:53:17.420
Which we were juggling a few episodes.
当时我们同时在拍好几集。

1225
00:53:17.760 --> 00:53:18.200
We were.
确实是。

1226
00:53:18.360 --> 00:53:21.740
I think we had a—maybe that was the ultimatum scrim.
我想我们当时——也许那是《最后通牒》那一集的布景。

1227
00:53:21.880 --> 00:53:22.160
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1228
00:53:22.860 --> 00:53:23.880
Michael is pacing.
迈克尔在踱步。

1229
00:53:24.140 --> 00:53:24.960
He's waiting for Holly.
他在等霍莉。

1230
00:53:25.220 --> 00:53:32.240
He is so anxious about her arrival, and then he realizes, oh, my God, there is a fake Christmas tree.
他为她的到来感到非常焦虑，然后他意识到，天哪，竟然有一棵假圣诞树。

1231
00:53:32.240 --> 00:53:35.120
And you can't have a fake Christmas tree at Classy Christmas.
在“高雅圣诞节”上怎么能用假圣诞树呢。

1232
00:53:35.120 --> 00:53:38.260
And especially not for someone who's from New Hampshire.
尤其是对于一个来自新罕布什尔州的人来说。

1233
00:53:38.500 --> 00:53:40.480
Good Lord, get rid of that tree.
天哪，赶紧把那棵树弄走。

1234
00:53:40.860 --> 00:53:45.320
So he's going to give Pam some money and send her out immediately for a real tree.
所以他给了帕姆一些钱，让她立刻去买一棵真树。

1235
00:53:45.600 --> 00:53:51.040
And now to up the Classy notch on this Christmas party, Michael has hired a bassiSt.
为了提升这次圣诞派对的“高雅”档次，迈克尔还雇了一位贝斯手。

1236
00:53:51.040 --> 00:53:58.300
Yes, he has hired one bassist for the entire day rather than an entire orchestra for 30 minutes.
没错，他雇了一位贝斯手弹一整天，而不是雇一整个管弦乐队弹30分钟。

1237
00:53:58.560 --> 00:53:58.860
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1238
00:53:59.680 --> 00:54:01.680
He's maybe regretting his choice.
他可能有点后悔自己的选择了。

1239
00:54:02.160 --> 00:54:04.360
The bass player was Jonathan Pintoff.
那位贝斯手是乔纳森·平托夫。

1240
00:54:04.560 --> 00:54:11.700
I went to his IMDb, Angela, and this is the only thing that Jonathan has ever appeared in, is this one episode of The Office.
安吉拉，我查了他的IMDb，这是乔纳森唯一出演过的作品，就是这一集《办公室》。

1241
00:54:12.000 --> 00:54:18.440
So I reached out to Randy Cordray to get some more information on him, and I will share that next week in Classy Christmas Part 2.
所以我联系了兰迪·科德雷想了解更多信息，下周在《高雅圣诞节（下）》里我会分享给大家。

1242
00:54:18.660 --> 00:54:20.000
I look forward to it.
我很期待。

1243
00:54:20.000 --> 00:54:22.840
But I have a busted catch.
但我发现了一个穿帮。

1244
00:54:23.200 --> 00:54:23.920
What's that?
是什么？

1245
00:54:24.200 --> 00:54:28.880
13 minutes, 16 seconds, when Pam asks if anyone wants to buy a Christmas tree with her.
在13分16秒，当帕姆问有没有人想跟她一起去买圣诞树时。

1246
00:54:29.800 --> 00:54:32.100
John Krasinski is not in character.
约翰·卡拉辛斯基没在状态。

1247
00:54:32.340 --> 00:54:35.700
I think he's chatting across the bullpen to Brian Baumgartner.
我觉得他当时正在办公区对面和布莱恩·鲍姆加特纳聊天。

1248
00:54:36.140 --> 00:54:36.500
Really?
真的吗？

1249
00:54:36.580 --> 00:54:38.860
They're probably talking fantasy football or something.
他们可能在聊梦幻足球之类的东西。

1250
00:54:39.060 --> 00:54:39.700
He's animated.
他看起来很兴奋。

1251
00:54:39.700 --> 00:54:41.180
He's talking to someone off camera.
他在和镜头外的人说话。

1252
00:54:41.400 --> 00:54:42.640
I'll put it in stories.
我会把它发到快拍里。

1253
00:54:42.900 --> 00:54:45.340
In fact, I have a double whammy here on JK.
事实上，关于JK，我这儿有个双重猛料。

1254
00:54:45.340 --> 00:54:55.560
Because then at 13 minutes, 34 seconds, when Andy says, my brid, instead of his hybrid, my brid, the tree won't fit into my brid.
因为在13分34秒，当安迪说“我的混动”时，他把“hybrid”说成了“brid”，他说“我的brid”，树塞不进我的brid里。

1255
00:54:55.560 --> 00:54:58.920
Every time he said, my brid, John would break.
每次他说“我的brid”时，约翰都会笑场。

1256
00:54:59.080 --> 00:55:01.320
And you can see John trying not to laugh.
你可以看到约翰在努力憋笑。

1257
00:55:02.680 --> 00:55:09.020
Well, Andy is going to volunteer to go get a tree with Pam, but they need a pickup truck because of his brid.
安迪打算主动提出和帕姆一起去买树，但因为他的混动车，他们需要一辆皮卡。

1258
00:55:09.360 --> 00:55:10.700
They're going to go ask Daryl.
他们打算去问问达里尔。

1259
00:55:10.700 --> 00:55:17.560
Yeah, but it's not a good time to ask Daryl because he's on the phone with Jada, his daughter's mom, and it's not going well.
是啊，但现在不是问达里尔的好时机，因为他正在和女儿的妈妈杰达通电话，而且谈得不太顺利。

1260
00:55:18.480 --> 00:55:18.800
Yes.
是的。

1261
00:55:19.120 --> 00:55:25.600
At 14 minutes and one second, Daryl is speaking to Justine, who was played by Erica Phillips.
在14分01秒，达里尔正在和贾斯汀通话，这个角色由埃里卡·菲利普斯饰演。

1262
00:55:26.420 --> 00:55:30.300
We brought her in just for this day, set her up on an offstage microphone.
我们特意请她来拍这一天，并为她设置了一个场外麦克风。

1263
00:55:30.700 --> 00:55:33.040
She is an amazing comedy actress.
她是一位出色的喜剧演员。

1264
00:55:33.040 --> 00:55:39.260
She's been on Veep, Arrested Development, Step Brothers, Superbad, The 40-Year-Old Virgin, and This is 40.
她出演过《副总统》、《发展受阻》、《非亲兄弟》、《太坏了》、《四十岁的老处男》和《四十而惑》。

1265
00:55:40.420 --> 00:55:44.220
And she will appear as Justine in season eight.
她将在第八季中以贾斯汀的身份出现。

1266
00:55:44.540 --> 00:55:45.600
We'll get to meet her.
我们到时候会见到她。

1267
00:55:46.440 --> 00:55:47.680
Andy's really going to lay it on thick.
安迪真的要开始死缠烂打了。

1268
00:55:47.800 --> 00:55:49.200
He's like, come on, Daryl, it'll be fun.
他就像是说，拜托，达里尔，会很有趣的。

1269
00:55:49.280 --> 00:55:50.760
We can do donuts in the snow.
我们可以在雪地里玩漂移。

1270
00:55:51.500 --> 00:55:55.600
I have a catch from this scene of Pam and Andy going into Daryl's office.
我从帕姆和安迪走进达里尔办公室的这一幕里发现了一个细节。

1271
00:55:55.760 --> 00:55:57.920
It's at 14 minutes and 30 seconds.
在14分30秒处。

1272
00:55:57.920 --> 00:56:04.860
It's Pam enters holding her coat, and she's wearing around her neck a black and tan winter scarf.
帕姆进门时手里拿着外套，脖子上围着一条黑棕相间的冬日围巾。

1273
00:56:05.820 --> 00:56:09.160
I just realized I took that scarf when we wrapped.
我刚意识到杀青的时候我把那条围巾拿走了。

1274
00:56:09.400 --> 00:56:10.100
You have it?
在你那儿？

1275
00:56:10.180 --> 00:56:16.340
Yeah, because I was just cleaning out my coat closet for the fall-winter season, and I found it in our scarf bin.
对，因为我刚才在清理秋冬季的衣柜，在我们的围巾箱里发现了它。

1276
00:56:16.460 --> 00:56:16.780
Aww.
噢。

1277
00:56:17.060 --> 00:56:22.000
So just add that to the list of things that I clearly randomly swiped from the set.
所以，把它加进我显然是从片场顺手牵羊拿走的东西清单里吧。

1278
00:56:23.820 --> 00:56:25.840
Toby has made it to the party.
托比已经到了派对现场。

1279
00:56:26.100 --> 00:56:27.080
Michael is pissed off.
迈克尔气坏了。

1280
00:56:27.080 --> 00:56:28.380
He doesn't want Toby at the party.
他不希望托比出现在派对上。

1281
00:56:28.560 --> 00:56:31.340
But Toby has had recess from the court.
但托比从法庭那边休庭过来了。

1282
00:56:31.780 --> 00:56:33.260
Everyone gathers around him.
大家都围在他身边。

1283
00:56:33.840 --> 00:56:36.820
They are hanging on his every word.
他们对他说的每一句话都洗耳恭听。

1284
00:56:37.120 --> 00:56:39.220
Toby is so delighted by this attention.
托比对这种关注感到非常高兴。

1285
00:56:39.600 --> 00:56:40.980
This scene was longer.
这一幕原本更长。

1286
00:56:41.160 --> 00:56:42.220
It's in deleted scenes.
在删减片段里。

1287
00:56:42.640 --> 00:56:44.500
Michael gets so jealous of him.
迈克尔对他嫉妒得要命。

1288
00:56:44.720 --> 00:56:45.440
We got to hear it.
我们得听听看。

1289
00:56:45.640 --> 00:56:51.340
Does he ever look at you and be like, don't you say another word or you're next?
他有没有盯着你看，然后说，你再多说一个字试试，下一个就是你？

1290
00:56:51.580 --> 00:56:53.440
It can get really tense.
气氛确实会变得很紧张。

1291
00:56:53.640 --> 00:56:53.900
Yeah.
是啊。

1292
00:56:54.420 --> 00:56:57.240
Yeah, I feel like I'm in an episode of Law and Order.
是啊，我觉得自己就像身处《法律与秩序》的一集里。

1293
00:56:58.060 --> 00:56:59.640
Well, the second half, right?
嗯，是后半部分吧？

1294
00:57:00.240 --> 00:57:00.640
Yeah.
没错。

1295
00:57:01.580 --> 00:57:02.760
That's pretty good, Toby.
那很不错，托比。

1296
00:57:03.980 --> 00:57:05.340
Hey, I'm proud of you.
嘿，我为你感到骄傲。

1297
00:57:05.500 --> 00:57:07.260
This is a great thing you're doing for this county.
你为这个县做了一件了不起的事。

1298
00:57:07.420 --> 00:57:07.640
Yes.
是的。

1299
00:57:07.840 --> 00:57:08.160
Yeah.
是啊。

1300
00:57:08.160 --> 00:57:09.560
Well, thanks, Oscar.
嗯，谢谢你，奥斯卡。

1301
00:57:11.040 --> 00:57:12.700
Man, it's hard not to talk about.
天哪，这事儿真难忍住不说。

1302
00:57:13.080 --> 00:57:17.880
If you say another word to anyone about this trial, I will kill you.
如果你再跟任何人提起这场审判，我就杀了你。

1303
00:57:18.300 --> 00:57:20.080
And good luck finding a jury for that.
而且祝你能找到愿意接这案子的陪审团。

1304
00:57:20.260 --> 00:57:21.720
Because no one will be impartial.
因为没人能做到公正无私。

1305
00:57:24.900 --> 00:57:25.300
Okay?
好吗？

1306
00:57:25.300 --> 00:57:30.790
I'm so jealous.
我太嫉妒了。

1307
00:57:31.590 --> 00:57:36.870
This continues on to A Talking Head That Aired, where Toby says he knows they're only talking
接下来是“已播出的访谈片段”，托比说他知道大家找他聊天

1308
00:57:36.870 --> 00:57:37.850
to him because of the trial.
只是因为那场审判。

1309
00:57:37.850 --> 00:57:38.890
But you know what?
但你知道吗？

1310
00:57:38.990 --> 00:57:41.030
One day, maybe they'll just be talking, right?
也许有一天，他们会单纯地找他聊天，对吧？

1311
00:57:41.770 --> 00:57:45.990
I had to go to Candy Bag Alts because I knew they would have some delicious ones for
我不得不去翻看“糖果袋”备选片段，因为我知道里面肯定有关于

1312
00:57:45.990 --> 00:57:46.310
Toby.
托比的精彩内容。

1313
00:57:46.910 --> 00:57:47.930
Here's one of them.
这是其中一段。

1314
00:57:48.850 --> 00:57:52.430
Toby, I never know what to say to people in social situations.
托比，我总不知道在社交场合该跟人说什么。

1315
00:57:52.670 --> 00:57:56.450
I usually take a shot of Jägermeister that I keep in my glove compartment.
我通常会喝一口放在手套箱里的野格酒。

1316
00:57:56.450 --> 00:57:59.670
And then it says he's trying hard to make a joke.
然后剧本写着他正努力想讲个笑话。

1317
00:58:00.190 --> 00:58:02.910
Glove compartment, more like Jaeger compartment.
手套箱？不如叫野格箱吧。

1318
00:58:03.610 --> 00:58:04.990
Then he gets depressed.
接着他就陷入了抑郁。

1319
00:58:05.270 --> 00:58:05.730
See?
看到了吗？

1320
00:58:05.950 --> 00:58:07.810
That's the kind of thing I would normally say.
那正是我平时会说的话。

1321
00:58:08.110 --> 00:58:11.470
But jury duty, that's like my Jaeger shot.
但陪审团义务，就像我的那口野格酒一样。

1322
00:58:12.470 --> 00:58:18.140
Candy Bag Alts sometimes were so random.
“糖果袋”备选片段有时候真的很随机。

1323
00:58:19.320 --> 00:58:22.480
So up next, Jim is going to be waiting for Dwight in the parking lot.
接下来，吉姆要在停车场等德怀特。

1324
00:58:22.640 --> 00:58:24.440
I re-watched this episode with my daughter.
我和我女儿重温了这一集。

1325
00:58:24.680 --> 00:58:28.120
And she was like, Mom, the doors are locked.
她说，妈妈，门锁着呢。

1326
00:58:28.120 --> 00:58:30.180
She noticed the doors are chained.
她注意到门被锁链锁住了。

1327
00:58:30.900 --> 00:58:31.820
Jim gets this call.
吉姆接到了这个电话。

1328
00:58:32.040 --> 00:58:34.560
There's a weird snowman behind him.
他身后有个奇怪的雪人。

1329
00:58:34.840 --> 00:58:36.480
And oh my God.
天哪。

1330
00:58:37.300 --> 00:58:42.620
So here is my question, because Dwight is going to bust out of this snowman and start
所以我的问题是，因为德怀特一会儿要从雪人里冲出来，开始

1331
00:58:42.620 --> 00:58:48.260
pelting Jim with snowballs until Jim is in the fetal position on the ground.
用雪球猛砸吉姆，直到吉姆蜷缩在地上动弹不得。

1332
00:58:48.800 --> 00:58:50.340
Who chained the doors?
是谁锁的门？

1333
00:58:50.880 --> 00:58:52.940
Who built the snowman around him?
是谁在他周围堆的雪人？

1334
00:58:53.020 --> 00:58:54.940
You have to think he has an accomplice, Nate.
你肯定会觉得他有个同伙，内特。

1335
00:58:55.320 --> 00:58:55.800
Nate.
内特。

1336
00:58:56.060 --> 00:58:56.340
Yes.
没错。

1337
00:58:56.460 --> 00:58:57.120
It must be.
肯定是他。

1338
00:58:57.120 --> 00:58:59.560
We had a fan question from Bennett H.
我们收到了来自犹他州盐湖城的贝内特·H的粉丝提问。

1339
00:58:59.680 --> 00:59:00.740
in Salt Lake City, Utah.
盐湖城，犹他州。

1340
00:59:01.020 --> 00:59:03.960
How did you guys film the scene with Rain in the snowman?
你们当时是怎么拍摄雷恩在雪人里的那场戏的？

1341
00:59:04.140 --> 00:59:06.860
Was he actually in the snowman?
他真的在雪人里面吗？

1342
00:59:07.840 --> 00:59:08.760
Yes, Bennett.
是的，贝内特。

1343
00:59:09.140 --> 00:59:10.560
Rain was in the snowman.
雷恩确实在雪人里。

1344
00:59:10.680 --> 00:59:11.840
Isn't that amazing?
这不是很神奇吗？

1345
00:59:12.240 --> 00:59:13.480
But let me back up.
但让我先退回一点讲。

1346
00:59:13.880 --> 00:59:20.780
I'm going to start by saying that Rain shared that it was in the high 90s during this scene
我得先说，雷恩分享过，拍这场戏的时候气温高达华氏90多度（约32摄氏度以上），

1347
00:59:20.780 --> 00:59:25.300
and blindingly sunny, the day that we shot all this stuff.
而且那天阳光刺眼，我们拍了所有这些镜头。

1348
00:59:25.760 --> 00:59:32.580
In post-production, they changed the color tone to look more gray, but it was just blistering
在后期制作中，他们把色调调成了灰色，但当时其实是酷热

1349
00:59:32.580 --> 00:59:32.960
heat.
难耐。

1350
00:59:33.880 --> 00:59:40.940
Randy said that because of the heat, creating this entire outdoor winter snow was a huge undertaking,
兰迪说，因为天气炎热，要在户外营造出这种冬日雪景是一项巨大的工程，

1351
00:59:41.300 --> 00:59:42.940
including these snowmen.
包括这些雪人。

1352
00:59:43.400 --> 00:59:50.000
Randy said they had to bring in an ice truck from Union Ice, an 18-wheeler tractor trailer,
兰迪说他们不得不从联合制冰公司调来一辆运冰卡车，是一辆18轮的半挂车，

1353
00:59:50.000 --> 00:59:55.080
and then they ran the ice through giant ice chippers to make all the snow.
然后他们用巨大的碎冰机把冰块打碎，制造出所有的雪。

1354
00:59:55.340 --> 01:00:00.940
He said that it kept melting, and they were constantly replacing the snow to keep the parking
他说雪一直在融化，他们不得不不断地补充雪，以保持停车场

1355
01:00:00.940 --> 01:00:01.960
lot covered in snow.
覆盖着雪。

1356
01:00:02.160 --> 01:00:05.880
He said it was a very slow process, very labor-intensive.
他说这是一个非常缓慢的过程，非常耗费人力。

1357
01:00:06.880 --> 01:00:14.240
Rain added that they had to give the entire crew UV protectant sunglasses to cut down on the glare
雷恩补充说，他们必须给全体工作人员配备防紫外线的太阳镜，以减少

1358
01:00:14.240 --> 01:00:17.880
from the snow and the sun from snow blindness.
雪地和阳光造成的刺眼光线，防止雪盲。

1359
01:00:18.760 --> 01:00:24.380
A set medic was on set, and the call sheet had this special note on it.
现场有一名随组医护人员，拍摄通告单上还有这样一条特别说明。

1360
01:00:24.540 --> 01:00:25.680
It said, quote,
上面写着，引用如下：

1361
01:00:25.880 --> 01:00:28.820
All crew, you will be working today in snow.
全体工作人员，你们今天将在雪地里工作。

1362
01:00:29.060 --> 01:00:30.480
Please wear appropriate shoes.
请穿合适的鞋子。

1363
01:00:30.800 --> 01:00:33.820
The weather forecast is for bright skies and hot weather.
天气预报显示今天晴空万里，天气炎热。

1364
01:00:34.100 --> 01:00:38.100
You will wear sunglasses to protect your eyes from the glare on the snow.
你们必须佩戴太阳镜，以保护眼睛免受雪地反光的伤害。

1365
01:00:38.380 --> 01:00:41.720
You would think they were probably just working in slush most of the day.
你可能会以为他们大部分时间都在泥泞中工作。

1366
01:00:41.720 --> 01:00:47.260
I mean, if you look carefully, there are a lot of puddles of water out there as well.
我的意思是，如果你仔细看，外面也有很多积水坑。

1367
01:00:47.460 --> 01:00:48.940
I mean, they were really fighting it.
我是说，他们真的在和环境作斗争。

1368
01:00:49.400 --> 01:00:52.720
You know, we shot these episodes over two weeks' time.
你知道，我们花了两个星期的时间拍摄这些剧集。

1369
01:00:53.740 --> 01:00:55.920
We shot all of this the first week.
第一周我们拍完了所有这些外景。

1370
01:00:56.580 --> 01:01:00.740
The second week, when we were shooting basically all indoors.
第二周，我们基本上都是在室内拍摄的。

1371
01:01:01.080 --> 01:01:01.680
Was it cooler?
那时候凉快点吗？

1372
01:01:01.880 --> 01:01:03.080
It was 72 degrees.
气温是72华氏度（约22摄氏度）。

1373
01:01:03.180 --> 01:01:04.060
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1374
01:01:04.340 --> 01:01:06.060
Yeah, we really should have flipped it.
是啊，我们真该把顺序调换一下。

1375
01:01:06.660 --> 01:01:08.480
But now let me get back to the snowmen.
但现在让我回到雪人的话题上来。

1376
01:01:09.100 --> 01:01:10.340
Here's how they did those.
这就是他们制作雪人的方法。

1377
01:01:10.340 --> 01:01:11.600
It was amazing.
太神奇了。

1378
01:01:11.800 --> 01:01:15.540
Randy Cordray sent us a video of how they made this snowman.
兰迪·科德雷给我们发了一段视频，展示了他们是如何制作这个雪人的。

1379
01:01:15.740 --> 01:01:20.060
And Angela will be putting that over on the Office Ladies Pod Instagram.
安吉拉会把它发布到《办公室女士》播客的Instagram上。

1380
01:01:20.440 --> 01:01:22.840
Randy, I always love the little nuggets you give me.
兰迪，我总是很喜欢你给我的这些小料。

1381
01:01:23.360 --> 01:01:30.040
They were built using a frame of metal wire mesh that could quickly be filled with chipped ice.
它们是用金属丝网框架搭建的，可以快速填满碎冰。

1382
01:01:30.040 --> 01:01:32.440
And they made a hollowed-out snowman.
他们做了一个空心的雪人。

1383
01:01:33.700 --> 01:01:37.980
But they were partially open in the back, which is why we only shot it from the front.
但它们的背面是半开放的，这就是为什么我们只从正面拍摄。

1384
01:01:38.260 --> 01:01:40.120
So rain could get inside.
这样雷恩才能钻进去。

1385
01:01:40.120 --> 01:01:43.660
They never fully enclosed him in snow.
他们从来没有把雪人完全封死。

1386
01:01:43.880 --> 01:01:45.640
There was always a way for him to exit.
总是留有让他出来的出口。

1387
01:01:46.620 --> 01:01:49.240
But they could make one in less than 10 minutes.
但他们可以在不到10分钟内就做一个出来。

1388
01:01:49.760 --> 01:01:50.020
Wow.
哇。

1389
01:01:50.380 --> 01:01:56.720
It was truly brilliant, the engineering of that, which was important because, you know, we had to do multiple takes.
这确实非常巧妙，这种工程设计很重要，因为你知道，我们必须进行多次拍摄。

1390
01:01:56.920 --> 01:01:57.080
Right.
没错。

1391
01:01:57.740 --> 01:02:03.580
Dwight is going to have a talking head that says he lacks the feeling in his fingers and penis, but he thought it was worth it.
德怀特有一个采访镜头，说他手指和阴茎都冻得没知觉了，但他觉得很值得。

1392
01:02:03.660 --> 01:02:03.940
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1393
01:02:04.460 --> 01:02:06.180
There was a candy bag alt.
还有一个关于糖果袋的备选方案。

1394
01:02:06.500 --> 01:02:06.980
Oh, tell.
哦，快说。

1395
01:02:07.500 --> 01:02:08.540
Oh, it's so good.
哦，太棒了。

1396
01:02:23.900 --> 01:02:29.290
Isn't that so good?
是不是很棒？

1397
01:02:29.450 --> 01:02:30.050
I love it.
我喜欢。

1398
01:02:30.590 --> 01:02:31.830
We're now going to see Jim.
我们现在要看到吉姆了。

1399
01:02:31.950 --> 01:02:32.890
He's bloodied.
他满身是血。

1400
01:02:33.150 --> 01:02:33.510
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1401
01:02:33.630 --> 01:02:34.630
He's in the kitchen.
他在厨房里。

1402
01:02:34.910 --> 01:02:35.270
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1403
01:02:35.450 --> 01:02:39.310
And he's just said he just kept throwing and throwing them at him.
他说他当时一直在朝他扔东西。

1404
01:02:39.370 --> 01:02:40.870
And then he gets a text from Dwight.
然后他收到了德怀特发来的短信。

1405
01:02:40.950 --> 01:02:42.150
How about icing it, LOL?
要不要冰敷一下，哈哈？

1406
01:02:42.670 --> 01:02:44.890
Well, listen, the time has arrived.
听着，时候到了。

1407
01:02:45.470 --> 01:02:46.410
Holly is here.
霍莉来了。

1408
01:02:46.410 --> 01:02:48.230
She's carrying a couple of boxes.
她搬着几个箱子。

1409
01:02:48.610 --> 01:02:48.870
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1410
01:02:49.110 --> 01:02:52.430
She asked Aaron for some help, but Aaron is not available.
她找亚伦帮忙，但亚伦没空。

1411
01:02:52.610 --> 01:02:54.710
She's waiting for her boss's pretty friend to arrive.
她在等她老板的漂亮朋友过来。

1412
01:02:55.870 --> 01:02:56.390
Aaron.
亚伦。

1413
01:02:56.690 --> 01:02:56.910
Aaron.
亚伦。

1414
01:02:57.310 --> 01:02:57.530
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1415
01:02:58.190 --> 01:03:00.610
When Michael sees Holly, it is so pure.
当迈克尔见到霍莉时，那场面太纯粹了。

1416
01:03:00.870 --> 01:03:02.210
It is so sweet.
太甜蜜了。

1417
01:03:02.490 --> 01:03:09.810
And if any of you guys have doubted that these two were meant for each other, I need you to hear how they greet one another.
如果你们中有人怀疑过他们俩是天生一对，我需要你们听听他们是怎么打招呼的。

1418
01:03:10.030 --> 01:03:11.010
We have to hear it.
我们必须得听听。

1419
01:03:11.610 --> 01:03:12.110
Hello?
喂？

1420
01:03:13.130 --> 01:03:14.430
Well, well, well.
哟，哟，哟。

1421
01:03:14.430 --> 01:03:17.590
Well, it isn't Michael Scott, you old bastard.
这不是迈克尔·斯科特吗，你这老混蛋。

1422
01:03:19.170 --> 01:03:23.590
I never thought I'd see your face around these parts, you old bastard.
我从没想过还能在这儿见到你，你这老混蛋。

1423
01:03:23.850 --> 01:03:26.410
Well, I did show my face around these parts, you old bastard.
我这不是在这儿露面了吗，你这老混蛋。

1424
01:03:26.570 --> 01:03:28.730
Why, you're some sort of wise guy, huh?
哟，你还挺会贫嘴的嘛，嗯？

1425
01:03:29.030 --> 01:03:30.050
I most certainly am.
我当然是。

1426
01:03:30.410 --> 01:03:31.530
Knock, knock, knock, knock, knock, knock.
敲敲敲敲敲敲。

1427
01:03:31.530 --> 01:03:34.630
Oh, homie.
噢，老兄。

1428
01:03:34.890 --> 01:03:35.270
Okay.
好吧。

1429
01:03:36.150 --> 01:03:37.170
Holly's back.
霍莉回来了。

1430
01:03:39.090 --> 01:03:39.770
Hi.
嗨。

1431
01:03:40.210 --> 01:03:40.670
Hi.
嗨。

1432
01:03:41.350 --> 01:03:43.510
There's still the hug monster, too.
还有拥抱怪兽呢。

1433
01:03:43.770 --> 01:03:44.730
The hug monster happens.
拥抱怪兽出现了。

1434
01:03:44.730 --> 01:03:49.190
In the script, it said that Holly immediately starts talking to him as Clint Eastwood.
剧本里写着霍莉立刻开始模仿克林特·伊斯特伍德跟他说话。

1435
01:03:49.330 --> 01:03:49.630
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1436
01:03:50.090 --> 01:03:54.530
And Michael then switches them to the Three Stooges, and then they go to Homer and Bart Simpson.
然后迈克尔把他们切换成了“三个臭皮匠”，接着他们又变成了荷马和巴特·辛普森。

1437
01:03:54.530 --> 01:03:56.950
We got a fan question from Carlos L.
我们收到了来自华盛顿州塔科马市卡洛斯·L的粉丝提问。

1438
01:03:57.310 --> 01:03:58.430
in Tacoma, Washington.
在塔科马，华盛顿州。

1439
01:03:59.310 --> 01:04:06.050
Why does Holly bring an entire box of her plaques and desk stuff and even put stuff on the wall if she's only going to be there for a week?
为什么霍莉只待一周却带了一整箱奖牌和办公用品，甚至还往墙上挂东西？

1440
01:04:06.050 --> 01:04:07.710
Oh, that's such a good point.
噢，这问题问得太好了。

1441
01:04:08.450 --> 01:04:12.650
It is, but Carlos, I would bring two boxes of stuff for a one-week job.
确实，但卡洛斯，如果是我去干一周的工作，我也会带两箱东西。

1442
01:04:13.070 --> 01:04:13.990
I would do that.
我会那么做的。

1443
01:04:14.170 --> 01:04:17.670
I would fully decorate my desk if I had a temp job and I had many.
如果我有临时工作，我绝对会把办公桌装饰得满满当当，我以前干过很多次。

1444
01:04:17.950 --> 01:04:18.350
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1445
01:04:18.830 --> 01:04:20.370
I like a homie desk.
我喜欢有归属感的办公桌。

1446
01:04:20.850 --> 01:04:22.370
I like a homie desk, too.
我也喜欢有归属感的办公桌。

1447
01:04:22.450 --> 01:04:24.430
I think two boxes is a little ambitious.
我觉得带两箱东西有点太雄心勃勃了。

1448
01:04:24.810 --> 01:04:27.690
Well, one box is work and the other box is decor.
嗯，一箱是工作用品，另一箱是装饰品。

1449
01:04:28.050 --> 01:04:29.090
I think it works.
我觉得这很合理。

1450
01:04:29.790 --> 01:04:33.470
Well, Kevin is going to ask Holly if she brought them anything for Nashua.
凯文打算问问霍莉有没有从纳舒厄给他们带什么东西。

1451
01:04:33.990 --> 01:04:37.310
She says she brought them some maple candy but ate some of it on the drive.
她说她带了一些枫糖糖果给他们，但在开车来的路上吃掉了一些。

1452
01:04:37.670 --> 01:04:40.650
Please go to 17 minutes, 52 seconds.
请跳转到17分52秒。

1453
01:04:40.990 --> 01:04:46.910
Because Kevin's look to camera when Holly says she ate most of the candy is so good.
因为当霍莉说她吃掉了大部分糖果时，凯文看向镜头的那个表情太棒了。

1454
01:04:47.510 --> 01:04:51.050
Well, later she tells Aaron that she can put some of the candy out.
嗯，后来她告诉亚伦，她可以拿出一些糖果来。

1455
01:04:51.370 --> 01:04:51.770
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1456
01:04:51.910 --> 01:04:54.650
And Aaron goes, so six pieces for the whole office?
然后亚伦说，所以整个办公室就六块？

1457
01:04:54.910 --> 01:04:54.990
Yeah.
是啊。

1458
01:04:55.790 --> 01:04:56.090
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1459
01:04:56.390 --> 01:04:57.270
A little Aaron sass.
亚伦的小小毒舌。

1460
01:04:57.690 --> 01:04:59.250
Michael can't get enough of Holly.
迈克尔对霍莉简直爱不释手。

1461
01:04:59.530 --> 01:05:01.230
They walk back to her desk together.
他们一起走回她的办公桌。

1462
01:05:01.410 --> 01:05:02.410
They're chatting away.
他们聊得很开心。

1463
01:05:02.410 --> 01:05:06.610
And this is when Michael finds out that Holly is still with AJ.
就在这时，迈克尔发现霍莉还在和AJ交往。

1464
01:05:07.010 --> 01:05:07.710
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1465
01:05:07.950 --> 01:05:09.610
He's given her a Woody doll.
他送了她一个胡迪玩偶。

1466
01:05:09.850 --> 01:05:10.730
He put it on her bed.
他把它放在了她的床上。

1467
01:05:10.850 --> 01:05:12.350
Michael's like, that's kind of creepy.
迈克尔觉得，这有点毛骨悚然。

1468
01:05:12.710 --> 01:05:14.550
And then she's like, well, what do you mean?
然后她说，好吧，你是什么意思？

1469
01:05:14.550 --> 01:05:15.370
We live together.
我们住在一起。

1470
01:05:15.970 --> 01:05:17.410
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1471
01:05:17.690 --> 01:05:17.910
Yeah.
是啊。

1472
01:05:18.490 --> 01:05:20.390
Heartbreak in human resources.
人力资源部的心碎时刻。

1473
01:05:20.710 --> 01:05:21.210
Major.
重大的那种。

1474
01:05:21.650 --> 01:05:24.910
We had a fan question from Natasha C in Dallas, Texas.
我们收到了一位来自德克萨斯州达拉斯的粉丝娜塔莎·C的提问。

1475
01:05:24.910 --> 01:05:29.570
Did you guys have to get special permission to use the Disney Woody doll?
你们当时是否需要获得特别许可才能使用迪士尼的胡迪玩偶？

1476
01:05:29.570 --> 01:05:32.610
And did you have to pay to use the Disney character?
而且你们是否需要付费才能使用这个迪士尼角色？

1477
01:05:34.050 --> 01:05:37.170
Remember how easy it was for us to get clearance for Hello Kitty?
还记得我们获得Hello Kitty的授权有多容易吗？

1478
01:05:37.170 --> 01:05:39.770
I'm going to say not this time.
我想说这次可没那么容易。

1479
01:05:40.030 --> 01:05:42.110
Not so much on the Woody doll.
胡迪玩偶的情况就没那么顺利了。

1480
01:05:42.370 --> 01:05:45.390
It was not a problem with Disney.
迪士尼那边倒是没问题。

1481
01:05:45.650 --> 01:05:48.270
They gave us permission to use the doll for free.
他们免费授权我们使用这个玩偶。

1482
01:05:48.450 --> 01:05:53.170
But NBCUniversal forbid us from featuring it.
但NBC环球禁止我们展示它。

1483
01:05:53.290 --> 01:05:56.310
They did not want to promote merchandise from another studio.
他们不想宣传其他制片厂的周边商品。

1484
01:05:56.870 --> 01:06:04.050
So Greg and Mindy called our NBC studio creative liaison, Lauren Anderson, who got involved.
所以格雷格和敏迪联系了我们NBC制片厂的创意联络人劳伦·安德森，她介入了此事。

1485
01:06:04.530 --> 01:06:09.570
Lauren took up the case with legal and sales, and eventually we got permission to use it.
劳伦向法务和销售部门争取，最终我们获得了使用许可。

1486
01:06:09.950 --> 01:06:12.970
I just love how Greg would always fight for the creative idea.
我真的很喜欢格雷格总是为创意想法据理力争的样子。

1487
01:06:13.710 --> 01:06:18.410
Because I think I would so easily think, oh, well, I guess we have to change it.
因为我觉得换做是我，很容易就会想，哦，好吧，我想我们只能改掉它了。

1488
01:06:18.450 --> 01:06:19.710
Yeah, I'll pick something else.
是啊，我会选点别的。

1489
01:06:19.910 --> 01:06:20.150
Yeah.
是啊。

1490
01:06:20.570 --> 01:06:22.630
Yeah, he always rallied behind his writers.
没错，他总是坚定地支持他的编剧们。

1491
01:06:22.930 --> 01:06:23.150
Yeah.
是啊。

1492
01:06:23.790 --> 01:06:26.190
Cassie, are you still working on the clacky balls?
凯西，你还在弄那些咔哒球吗？

1493
01:06:26.790 --> 01:06:27.890
I'm making progress.
我正在取得进展。

1494
01:06:28.470 --> 01:06:30.510
I don't know if it'll be done by the end of the episode.
我不知道在这一集结束前能不能弄好。

1495
01:06:30.570 --> 01:06:31.630
Have you freed a ball?
你解开一个球了吗？

1496
01:06:31.870 --> 01:06:35.310
I haven't freed a ball, but the knot is so much looser.
我还没解开球，但结已经松动多了。

1497
01:06:36.450 --> 01:06:41.430
I think I'm now at the point of what the four-year-old did, and I'm just trying to, like, untangle.
我觉得我现在已经到了那个四岁小孩做到的程度，我只是在尝试解开它。

1498
01:06:41.670 --> 01:06:42.010
Okay.
好吧。

1499
01:06:42.310 --> 01:06:42.450
Wow.
哇。

1500
01:06:42.550 --> 01:06:44.870
Well, I will leave it with you.
好吧，那就交给你了。

1501
01:06:45.130 --> 01:06:48.810
Of all the people that have tried, you are showing the most passion and dedication.
在所有尝试过的人中，你展现出了最强的热情和奉献精神。

1502
01:06:49.430 --> 01:06:51.130
Well, I'm not hanging out at your house.
好吧，我可没在你家闲逛。

1503
01:06:51.130 --> 01:06:52.350
I'm listening to a podcaSt.
我在听播客。

1504
01:06:54.610 --> 01:06:59.150
Pam, Andy, and Daryl are at the Christmas tree lot, and Daryl is continuing to argue with his ex,
帕姆、安迪和达里尔在圣诞树售卖点，达里尔还在和他的前任争吵，

1505
01:06:59.350 --> 01:07:04.090
and Pam really decides she's going to make this Christmas special for Daryl and Jada.
而帕姆决定一定要为达里尔和贾达过一个特别的圣诞节。

1506
01:07:04.270 --> 01:07:05.330
She's going to step in.
她打算插手了。

1507
01:07:05.330 --> 01:07:05.750
Yeah.
没错。

1508
01:07:05.890 --> 01:07:07.950
She says, why don't you bring her to the party?
她说，你为什么不带她来参加派对呢？

1509
01:07:08.190 --> 01:07:09.170
It'll be fun.
会很有趣的。

1510
01:07:09.270 --> 01:07:12.350
There'll be Santa and music, and it'll be great.
会有圣诞老人和音乐，一定会很棒。

1511
01:07:12.630 --> 01:07:14.250
You'll be able to dazzle her.
你一定能让她眼前一亮。

1512
01:07:14.850 --> 01:07:16.910
Jenna, I have a location question for you.
珍娜，我有个关于拍摄地点的问题想问你。

1513
01:07:17.090 --> 01:07:17.510
Yes?
什么事？

1514
01:07:17.730 --> 01:07:18.850
Where was this tree lot?
这个树木售卖点是在哪儿？

1515
01:07:19.250 --> 01:07:25.450
Angela, when I watched this episode, my memory was that this tree lot was built in our parking lot.
安吉拉，我看这一集的时候，记忆中这个树木售卖点就是搭在我们停车场里的。

1516
01:07:25.850 --> 01:07:26.370
Yes!
没错！

1517
01:07:26.390 --> 01:07:28.490
I remember them moving cars and stuff.
我记得他们挪动了汽车之类的东西。

1518
01:07:28.690 --> 01:07:29.210
Yeah.
是啊。

1519
01:07:29.210 --> 01:07:31.730
I asked Randy, is my memory correct?
我问了兰迪，我的记忆对吗？

1520
01:07:31.890 --> 01:07:33.310
And he said, it is!
他说，是对的！

1521
01:07:33.790 --> 01:07:38.450
He also told me that we rented all of those trees from that company Green Set.
他还告诉我，我们是从那家叫“绿色布景”的公司租来的所有树。

1522
01:07:38.630 --> 01:07:42.030
Remember the people who put a fake iceberg in your lawn for you?
还记得那些帮你把假冰山放在草坪上的人吗？

1523
01:07:42.250 --> 01:07:43.850
Yeah, that's where we got all the trees.
对，我们就是从那儿弄来的所有树。

1524
01:07:44.050 --> 01:07:47.430
So I did not have to go far to go on this tree lot.
所以我根本不用走远就能去这个树木售卖点。

1525
01:07:47.670 --> 01:07:50.190
Well, they're going to arrive back to the bullpen.
好了，他们要回到办公区了。

1526
01:07:50.470 --> 01:07:52.290
They've picked up Jada, I guess.
我想他们已经接上贾达了。

1527
01:07:52.530 --> 01:07:54.050
Yeah, and guess what?
是啊，你猜怎么着？

1528
01:07:54.210 --> 01:07:54.470
What?
怎么了？

1529
01:07:54.470 --> 01:07:55.950
There's no jolly Santa.
没有快乐的圣诞老人。

1530
01:07:56.290 --> 01:07:59.730
There's just snarky, sad, sassy Santa.
只有尖酸、忧郁、傲慢的圣诞老人。

1531
01:08:00.110 --> 01:08:00.590
Yes.
没错。

1532
01:08:00.850 --> 01:08:04.750
I want to give a shout-out to Taylor Holliman, who played Jada.
我想向饰演贾达的泰勒·霍利曼致敬。

1533
01:08:04.970 --> 01:08:09.690
She was with us for three episodes of The Office, and she also appeared on Community and New Girl.
她和我们一起拍了三集《办公室》，她还出演过《废柴联盟》和《杰茜驾到》。

1534
01:08:10.050 --> 01:08:10.650
She was great.
她演得太棒了。

1535
01:08:11.050 --> 01:08:16.370
I mean, the thing that's crazy is when you see all of the actors that were kids and see them now,
我是说，最疯狂的是当你看到所有曾经是童星的演员，再看看现在的他们，

1536
01:08:16.550 --> 01:08:18.190
that's when I really feel old.
那时候我才真的觉得自己老了。

1537
01:08:18.290 --> 01:08:18.970
I know.
我懂。

1538
01:08:19.770 --> 01:08:23.090
Well, the ladies have decided to chat Holly up.
好吧，女士们决定去和霍莉聊聊。

1539
01:08:23.090 --> 01:08:27.130
They want the DTR, as we used to call it in college.
她们想进行“DTR”，就像我们大学时常说的那样。

1540
01:08:27.330 --> 01:08:28.410
What's the DTR?
什么是DTR？

1541
01:08:28.810 --> 01:08:30.190
Define the relationship.
定义关系。

1542
01:08:30.510 --> 01:08:32.890
Oh, I've never heard that.
哦，我从没听说过这个词。

1543
01:08:32.930 --> 01:08:34.470
Have you had the DTR?
你进行过DTR吗？

1544
01:08:34.810 --> 01:08:36.790
That means, have you locked it down?
那意思是，你们确定关系了吗？

1545
01:08:36.810 --> 01:08:37.790
What are the labels?
标签是什么？

1546
01:08:37.810 --> 01:08:38.730
We need to know.
我们需要知道。

1547
01:08:38.910 --> 01:08:46.510
Well, we find out that AJ has not proposed, even though maybe Holly would like him to?
好吧，我们发现AJ还没有求婚，尽管霍莉可能希望他求婚？

1548
01:08:46.790 --> 01:08:47.910
I think she would.
我觉得她是希望的。

1549
01:08:48.110 --> 01:08:49.950
That's what I feel like she's hinting at.
我觉得她就是在暗示这一点。

1550
01:08:50.030 --> 01:08:50.730
They've moved in.
他们已经同居了。

1551
01:08:50.870 --> 01:08:51.790
She wants to have kids.
她想要孩子。

1552
01:08:51.790 --> 01:08:53.070
They've been together a year.
他们在一起一年了。

1553
01:08:53.370 --> 01:08:55.270
Kelly says you need to give them an ultimatum.
凯利说你需要给他们下最后通牒。

1554
01:08:55.890 --> 01:08:57.330
And Pam's like, wait, wait, wait, guys.
然后帕姆说，等等，等等，伙计们。

1555
01:08:57.450 --> 01:09:02.650
I don't know if we should be giving her relationship advice, but Holly takes it.
我不知道我们是否应该给她提供恋爱建议，但霍莉听进去了。

1556
01:09:02.970 --> 01:09:08.870
I don't know if you notice, but I'm freezing in this scene because I had to take off my sweater.
我不知道你有没有注意到，我在这一幕里冻得要死，因为我不得不脱掉毛衣。

1557
01:09:08.870 --> 01:09:11.970
Oh, yeah, you're in the tank top to set up Dwight.
哦，对，你穿着背心是为了给德怀特设套。

1558
01:09:12.250 --> 01:09:12.570
Yes.
是的。

1559
01:09:13.570 --> 01:09:17.010
I mean, when I watched this scene, I could see that I was freezing.
我是说，当我回看这一幕时，我能看出我当时冻坏了。

1560
01:09:17.190 --> 01:09:19.370
I have my arms crossed across the front of my body.
我双臂交叉抱在身前。

1561
01:09:19.410 --> 01:09:21.490
I'm holding my hands in a fiSt.
我紧握着拳头。

1562
01:09:22.130 --> 01:09:24.310
I think you can see goosebumps on my arMs.
我想你能看到我手臂上的鸡皮疙瘩。

1563
01:09:24.930 --> 01:09:26.190
I was so cold.
我当时太冷了。

1564
01:09:26.390 --> 01:09:30.210
I got cold watching the scene just from the memory of how cold I was.
光是回想起当时有多冷，看这一幕时我就觉得冷。

1565
01:09:31.190 --> 01:09:33.790
I can't imagine being in a tank top on that set.
我无法想象在那个片场穿着背心是什么感觉。

1566
01:09:33.970 --> 01:09:34.190
No.
没错。

1567
01:09:34.210 --> 01:09:35.490
So I know you were cold.
所以我知道你当时很冷。

1568
01:09:36.070 --> 01:09:38.170
Holly would have had a talking head here.
霍莉本该在这里有一个采访镜头。

1569
01:09:38.330 --> 01:09:40.450
It was in the shooting draft, but was deleted.
剧本初稿里有，但被删掉了。

1570
01:09:40.850 --> 01:09:43.970
And there were also several candy bag alts for it.
而且为此还拍了好几个备选的即兴台词。

1571
01:09:44.190 --> 01:09:45.550
I'd like to read one of them.
我想读其中一个。

1572
01:09:45.670 --> 01:09:46.050
Please.
请吧。

1573
01:09:47.250 --> 01:09:49.370
Holly, it's not really an ultimatum.
霍莉，这其实不算最后通牒。

1574
01:09:49.530 --> 01:09:51.690
It's just a deadline with consequences.
这只是一个带有后果的截止日期。

1575
01:09:52.590 --> 01:09:53.770
I loved that.
我喜欢这个说法。

1576
01:09:54.050 --> 01:09:58.170
I'm not giving you an ultimatum, but I am giving you a deadline with big consequences.
我不是在给你下最后通牒，但我确实是在给你一个带有严重后果的截止日期。

1577
01:09:58.490 --> 01:10:00.870
You know, that sounds like healthy boundaries to me.
你知道，这听起来像是健康的界限。

1578
01:10:01.690 --> 01:10:03.010
I like that framing.
我喜欢这种表述方式。

1579
01:10:03.970 --> 01:10:08.130
Pam's going to walk back to her desk, which is very confusing to Jim because he was pretty
帕姆走回她的办公桌，这让吉姆非常困惑，因为他很确定

1580
01:10:08.130 --> 01:10:10.930
sure that she was sitting at her desk, but it's not her.
她应该坐在桌前，但那不是她。

1581
01:10:11.170 --> 01:10:16.110
It's Dwight in a Pam wig wearing Pam's sweater, and he starts pelting Jim with snowballs.
那是戴着帕姆假发、穿着帕姆毛衣的德怀特，他开始用雪球砸吉姆。

1582
01:10:16.790 --> 01:10:20.510
Yeah, we find out, I guess, that Dwight has wigs for every person in the office because
是的，我想我们发现德怀特有办公室里每个人的假发，因为

1583
01:10:20.510 --> 01:10:21.510
you just never know.
你永远不知道会发生什么。

1584
01:10:22.570 --> 01:10:23.890
I have a question for you.
我有个问题想问你。

1585
01:10:24.030 --> 01:10:24.470
What is it?
什么问题？

1586
01:10:24.650 --> 01:10:27.330
Was that really Pam's sweater, or did they get him another sweater?
那真的是帕姆的毛衣吗，还是他们又给他找了件毛衣？

1587
01:10:27.690 --> 01:10:30.210
No, they squeezed him into my sweater.
不，他们硬把他塞进了我的毛衣里。

1588
01:10:30.550 --> 01:10:31.110
Okay.
好吧。

1589
01:10:31.430 --> 01:10:31.690
Yes.
是的。

1590
01:10:31.910 --> 01:10:34.930
The arms were very, very tight on him.
袖子在他身上勒得非常非常紧。

1591
01:10:35.190 --> 01:10:40.810
Both Mindy and Kim Ferry talked about this wig sequence on officetelly.com.
敏迪和金·费里都在officetelly.com上谈论过这个假发片段。

1592
01:10:41.330 --> 01:10:42.310
Mindy said,
敏迪说，

1593
01:10:42.310 --> 01:10:46.610
When I was writing this episode, I just thought how funny Rain would look in a Meredith wig.
当我写这一集时，我只是觉得雷恩戴着梅雷迪思的假发看起来会很滑稽。

1594
01:10:47.030 --> 01:10:52.090
And my stage direction for him was, he, quote, whips around like a dramatic hamster.
我对他的舞台指导是，他，引用一下，像一只戏剧性的仓鼠一样猛地转过身。

1595
01:10:53.070 --> 01:10:58.390
She said, the Stanley is probably my favorite because of the way Rain held up the crossword
她说，斯坦利的假发可能是她最喜欢的，因为雷恩拿着填字游戏的方式

1596
01:10:58.390 --> 01:10:59.990
puzzle with so much seriousness.
显得非常严肃。

1597
01:11:00.830 --> 01:11:07.470
Kim Ferry said that the direction she was given was that these wigs should not be perfect because
金·费里说她得到的指导是，这些假发不应该太完美，因为

1598
01:11:07.470 --> 01:11:10.110
Dwight would have made them himself on the farm.
德怀特应该是自己在农场里做的。

1599
01:11:10.330 --> 01:11:12.870
So they're a little bit off, but a close match.
所以它们看起来有点怪，但很像。

1600
01:11:13.270 --> 01:11:19.270
She also said that we did all those shots in really quick order and that she and Sherry Perry
她还说我们很快地拍完了所有镜头，她和雪莉·佩里

1601
01:11:19.270 --> 01:11:22.190
would rush in and put a new wig on, get the shot, and then do the next one.
就会冲进去换个新假发，拍完这一条，然后接着拍下一条。

1602
01:11:22.290 --> 01:11:23.290
It was all really faSt.
一切都进行得非常快。

1603
01:11:23.290 --> 01:11:24.510
I think we were on a deadline.
我想我们当时赶着进度。

1604
01:11:24.510 --> 01:11:29.990
Well, you'll see some great reactions of everyone because we were just reacting as ourselves.
嗯，你们会看到大家很棒的反应，因为我们当时只是在展现真实的自己。

1605
01:11:30.290 --> 01:11:33.610
Again, watch Phyllis's face as John gets pelted.
再说一次，注意看约翰被砸时菲利斯的表情。

1606
01:11:34.650 --> 01:11:39.330
And Jenna, I'm just going to need to know for future reference, what is a dramatic hamster?
还有珍娜，我为了以后参考需要问一下，什么是“戏剧性仓鼠”？

1607
01:11:39.650 --> 01:11:41.250
I think that's what you saw.
我想那就是你看到的那个。

1608
01:11:41.430 --> 01:11:42.770
Is that a meme or something?
那是个表情包之类的东西吗？

1609
01:11:43.190 --> 01:11:44.330
Dramatic hamster.
戏剧性仓鼠。

1610
01:11:44.450 --> 01:11:45.830
I feel like I have to Google that.
我觉得我得去谷歌搜一下。

1611
01:11:46.190 --> 01:11:50.070
Well, speaking of throwing snowballs, Jim has a plan.
说到扔雪球，吉姆有个计划。

1612
01:11:50.070 --> 01:11:57.870
He's got out his lacrosse stick, and he is looking in the conference room, waiting for his moment to pelt Dwight.
他拿出了长曲棍球杆，正盯着会议室，等待时机去砸德怀特。

1613
01:11:58.050 --> 01:12:01.130
And he's doing like a little back and forth swatty move, swatty move.
他做了一个来回挥舞的动作，挥舞动作。

1614
01:12:01.530 --> 01:12:03.990
It's like a prep move, swatty swat, swat, swat.
就像是预备动作，挥啊挥，挥，挥。

1615
01:12:04.050 --> 01:12:10.910
It begs the question, why does Jim have a lacrosse stick, and how did he get a hold of one on such short notice?
这就引出了一个问题，为什么吉姆会有长曲棍球杆，而且他是怎么在这么短的时间内弄到手的？

1616
01:12:11.110 --> 01:12:13.110
Maybe he keeps it in the trunk of his car.
也许他一直放在汽车后备箱里。

1617
01:12:13.110 --> 01:12:15.530
Maybe he plays like adult lacrosse on the weekends.
也许他周末会去打成人长曲棍球。

1618
01:12:15.990 --> 01:12:16.850
That's what I'm saying.
我就是这个意思。

1619
01:12:16.850 --> 01:12:23.090
I think it's weird that he has this on hand, but what he's going to do is he's going to put a snowball in this lacrosse stick.
我觉得他随身带着这个挺奇怪的，但他打算把一个雪球放进长曲棍球杆里。

1620
01:12:23.230 --> 01:12:24.250
He's going to whip it at Dwight.
他要把它甩向德怀特。

1621
01:12:24.330 --> 01:12:32.150
He's going to miss, and he's going to break the window, which is, for next week, going to make the party miserable because now the whole office is cold.
他会打偏，然后打破窗户，这会导致下周的派对变得很糟糕，因为现在整个办公室都冷飕飕的。

1622
01:12:32.510 --> 01:12:34.550
We had a fan question from Jennifer M.
我们收到一个来自奥兰多的詹妮弗·M的粉丝提问。

1623
01:12:34.650 --> 01:12:35.290
in Orlando.
在奥兰多。

1624
01:12:35.870 --> 01:12:40.490
My husband and I have debated for years about what Jim throws at Dwight.
我和我丈夫多年来一直争论吉姆到底扔了什么砸德怀特。

1625
01:12:40.490 --> 01:12:47.570
I say he threw a snowball, but my husband thinks he threw a lacrosse ball because a snowball wouldn't be strong enough to break the windows.
我说他扔的是雪球，但我丈夫认为他扔的是长曲棍球，因为雪球的威力不足以打破窗户。

1626
01:12:47.850 --> 01:12:50.310
Can you tell me what did Jim throw at Dwight?
你能告诉我吉姆到底扔了什么吗？

1627
01:12:51.050 --> 01:12:52.690
Well, Jennifer, you are correct.
嗯，詹妮弗，你是对的。

1628
01:12:52.690 --> 01:12:54.370
It was scripted as a snowball.
剧本里写的是雪球。

1629
01:12:54.770 --> 01:12:56.930
It said, Jim sees a shot.
上面写着，吉姆看到了机会。

1630
01:12:57.130 --> 01:12:58.270
He flings the snowball.
他甩出了雪球。

1631
01:12:58.270 --> 01:13:02.790
He misses, and it hits the glass window, which pops out a frame and falls out.
他没打中，雪球击中了玻璃窗，把窗框撞了出来，掉了下去。

1632
01:13:02.990 --> 01:13:03.930
People scream.
人们尖叫起来。

1633
01:13:04.510 --> 01:13:06.890
But they changed it to break the window.
但他们改成了打破窗户。

1634
01:13:07.950 --> 01:13:11.970
Randy said we used that old-timey candy glass, breakaway glass.
兰迪说我们用了那种老式糖果玻璃，也就是特技碎裂玻璃。

1635
01:13:12.510 --> 01:13:17.990
He said we had four panels ready to go, but John nailed it on the first take.
他说我们准备了四块玻璃，但约翰第一条就成功了。

1636
01:13:18.430 --> 01:13:18.730
Hmm.
嗯。

1637
01:13:19.250 --> 01:13:19.650
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1638
01:13:19.830 --> 01:13:20.990
And so it was a snowball.
所以那确实是个雪球。

1639
01:13:21.210 --> 01:13:21.470
Yes.
是的。

1640
01:13:21.470 --> 01:13:24.390
It was both scripted as a snowball and it was a snowball.
剧本里写的是雪球，实际用的也是雪球。

1641
01:13:24.690 --> 01:13:24.770
A real snowball.
一个真正的雪球。

1642
01:13:24.790 --> 01:13:26.350
I mean, we packed it tight.
我是说，我们把它捏得很紧。

1643
01:13:26.530 --> 01:13:28.110
It was an ice ball.
那是个冰球。

1644
01:13:28.290 --> 01:13:28.470
Right.
没错。

1645
01:13:28.670 --> 01:13:30.130
But it was not a lacrosse ball.
但那绝对不是长曲棍球。

1646
01:13:30.550 --> 01:13:33.310
Well, this episode is going to end with Michael.
好了，这一集将以迈克尔的镜头结束。

1647
01:13:33.310 --> 01:13:34.830
He's pretty sad, you guys.
伙计们，他挺难过的。

1648
01:13:35.230 --> 01:13:39.730
He says, I guess there's some people you stay together with when you transfer and some people
他说，我想有些人调职时会一起走，而有些人

1649
01:13:39.730 --> 01:13:40.310
you don't.
则不会。

1650
01:13:40.830 --> 01:13:42.650
And he can be mature about that.
他对此能表现得很成熟。

1651
01:13:42.910 --> 01:13:46.730
And then he pours a whole cup of coffee onto Woody in the trash.
然后他把整整一杯咖啡倒在了垃圾桶里的伍迪身上。

1652
01:13:46.910 --> 01:13:48.610
I was horrified by this.
我当时被吓坏了。

1653
01:13:49.330 --> 01:13:50.730
I was so upset.
我难过极了。

1654
01:13:50.870 --> 01:13:51.510
Were you really?
你真的吗？

1655
01:13:51.690 --> 01:13:52.090
Yes.
是的。

1656
01:13:52.570 --> 01:13:59.890
I do not believe in, what would you call that, vandalizing other people's property?
我不相信，怎么说呢，破坏别人的财产这种事？

1657
01:13:59.890 --> 01:14:01.530
An ex, you know?
前任，你懂的？

1658
01:14:01.710 --> 01:14:02.410
I would never.
我绝不会那样做。

1659
01:14:02.590 --> 01:14:06.790
I would never go key someone's car or, you know, set their clothes on fire.
我绝不会去划别人的车，或者，你知道，放火烧他们的衣服。

1660
01:14:06.870 --> 01:14:07.870
Of course not.
当然不会。

1661
01:14:08.170 --> 01:14:09.130
Or like pee on their clothes.
或者在他们的衣服上撒尿之类的。

1662
01:14:09.130 --> 01:14:09.770
I don't know.
我不知道。

1663
01:14:09.830 --> 01:14:11.090
You hear about people doing this stuff.
你总能听到有人做这种事。

1664
01:14:11.170 --> 01:14:12.050
Don't do that, people.
别那样做，各位。

1665
01:14:12.410 --> 01:14:13.230
Come on now.
拜托了。

1666
01:14:13.690 --> 01:14:14.550
Come on now.
拜托了。

1667
01:14:14.650 --> 01:14:15.730
I didn't care for it.
我不喜欢那样。

1668
01:14:15.970 --> 01:14:16.410
Yeah.
是啊。

1669
01:14:16.410 --> 01:14:17.670
I mean, it's very petty.
我是说，这太小家子气了。

1670
01:14:18.610 --> 01:14:19.410
Super petty.
超级小气。

1671
01:14:19.890 --> 01:14:21.050
And you know what?
而且你知道吗？

1672
01:14:21.390 --> 01:14:23.010
Holly's going to be ticked off about it.
霍莉肯定会为此气疯的。

1673
01:14:23.110 --> 01:14:23.910
And rightly so.
理应如此。

1674
01:14:23.910 --> 01:14:25.590
That's for next week.
那是下周的事了。

1675
01:14:25.770 --> 01:14:26.210
That's right.
没错。

1676
01:14:26.410 --> 01:14:27.590
Classy Christmas, too.
还有“优雅圣诞节”呢。

1677
01:14:27.830 --> 01:14:28.850
Don't mess with my Woody.
别动我的伍迪。

1678
01:14:30.310 --> 01:14:31.270
Oh, wow.
噢，哇。

1679
01:14:32.510 --> 01:14:34.990
And on that note, Cassie.
说到这个，凯西。

1680
01:14:35.450 --> 01:14:36.770
Any luck with the balls?
球弄好了吗？

1681
01:14:38.010 --> 01:14:39.070
It's still tangled.
还是缠在一起。

1682
01:14:39.590 --> 01:14:40.050
All right.
好吧。

1683
01:14:40.410 --> 01:14:41.790
It's tangled, but it's hanging lower.
虽然缠着，但垂得更低了。

1684
01:14:41.790 --> 01:14:42.870
It really is.
确实是。

1685
01:14:43.230 --> 01:14:43.590
Well.
好吧。

1686
01:14:43.750 --> 01:14:45.930
We'll have you work on that again next week.
下周再让你接着弄。

1687
01:14:46.210 --> 01:14:47.490
Cassie, good luck with the balls.
凯西，祝你搞定那些球。

1688
01:14:47.650 --> 01:14:48.490
We'll check in next week.
我们下周再来看看。

1689
01:14:48.490 --> 01:14:51.250
Before we go, would you like to see what they're referencing to the hamster?
在结束之前，你们想看看他们提到的那只仓鼠吗？

1690
01:14:51.510 --> 01:14:52.850
Oh, the dramatic hamster.
噢，那只戏剧性的仓鼠。

1691
01:14:52.850 --> 01:14:53.810
Is that a thing?
真有这个东西？

1692
01:14:54.070 --> 01:14:54.310
Yes.
是的。

1693
01:14:54.470 --> 01:14:55.430
It's classic old internet.
那是经典的早期互联网梗。

1694
01:14:55.710 --> 01:14:56.410
It's just this.
就是这个。

1695
01:15:00.040 --> 01:15:01.740
Yes, I remember this guy.
对，我记得这只仓鼠。

1696
01:15:02.360 --> 01:15:04.500
That's exactly what Dwight does.
德怀特做的动作一模一样。

1697
01:15:04.920 --> 01:15:07.540
Oh, you've got to do that side by side on Instagram.
